{
  "_comment": "Optional: every key has a default (common/catalog.py: the committed folds, CT_GAT/data, CT_GAT/cache/<dataset>), so a machine that unzips the collections into CT_GAT/data needs no datasets.json. Copy to datasets.json (gitignored) and edit the paths to override them on this machine; the order is environment variable, then this file, then the default. A relative path is relative to this file. 'cache' is the folder build_cache writes (samples/, index.csv, vocab.json); 'protocols' are the --protocol values that read it by default; --cache <name> picks a dataset by name, GT_CACHE (a folder) beats both. 'sources' are the raw inputs a cache is built from, and where runs go; each has an environment variable that wins (GT_BUNDLE, GT_COLLECTIONS, GT_FOLDS, GT_FOLDS_V3, GT_RUNS, GT_TEAM_B_BUILD).",

